```c
drm_dbg_kms(plane_state->plane->dev, "Cannot update plane of a disabled CRTC.\n");
drm_dbg_kms(plane_state->plane->dev, "Invalid scaling of plane\n");
drm_dbg_kms(plane_state->plane->dev, "Plane must cover entire CRTC\n");
```
Reason:
The fix involves changing the logging statements to reference the `plane` device instead of the `crtc` device. This ensures that the logging can still occur even when the `crtc` is NULL, thus preventing errors and allowing the function to handle cases where the `crtc` cannot be found.

